commit 61bed9dd
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-24 08:14:50 -0600
subject: feat(dashboard): add error boundaries with transient 429/5xx retry UI

Sweep confirmed zero error.js / global-error.js files existed anywhere
under src/app — all 29 dashboard pages fell through to Next.js's default
error screen on any uncaught render error.

- src/app/(dashboard)/error.js: dashboard-group boundary sitting INSIDE
  DashboardLayout so sidebar/header stay visible during a page error.
  Detects transient HTTP errors (429 / 5xx) via error.message/digest
  and shows targeted retry UI; generic fallback with reset + back-to-
  dashboard otherwise. Self-contained (inline buttons, no shared-
  component imports) so the boundary cannot be taken down by the same
  failure it catches.
- src/app/global-error.js: root fallback for errors escaping the group
  boundary (DashboardLayout itself, login, landing). Renders its own
  <html>/<body> with zero layout dependencies; uses a plain <a> (not
  next/link) deliberately since it renders outside the app-router
  context it is catching failures of.

Scope: covers render-time errors only. Ad-hoc fetch error handling
inside individual pages (alert(), silent .catch(() => {}), console.log)
is a separate cleanup not addressed here.

